.DS_Store
.idea/
bs1_audio/
bs1_gfx/
bs2_audio/
bs2_gfx/
# The soundtrack is MIDI beside a SoundFont, and the SoundFont is a big binary
# that need not be in a checkout. The audio logs are not that: they are level
# content, a couple of hundred kilobytes each, and a level that names one has
# nothing to play without it.
assets/audio/*
!assets/audio/logs/
doom_likes/
blake_stone/
*.exe
*.pk3
temp/
/goray
/go-fps

# F12 writes this while playing; it is a scratch capture, not an asset.
/screenshot00.png

# Every game and mod the asset migration reads, and the source of the engines
# that originally drew them, gathered by hand and moved here so re-migrate.sh
# needs no paths of its own. None of it is ours to ship: two commercial games off
# their own media, two mod releases, nine community weapons and three engine
# checkouts.
#
# The contents are ignored rather than the folder, so that the two files that
# *are* ours can stay: the README saying what belongs here and where each piece
# came from, and the go.mod that keeps the parent module's ./... from walking
# into gzdoom.
/3rd-party/*
!/3rd-party/README.md
!/3rd-party/go.mod

# Built tool binaries, from `go build ./tools/...` in the repo root.
/importss
/importbs
/mapgen
